   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Conditional inversion without wenn",
     "texto": [
      "In formal, legal German, the conditional conjunction **wenn** can be omitted. In that case the conjugated verb in Konjunktiv II moves to the absolute first position of the subordinate clause (**V1-Stellung**): **Hätten die Parteien früher verhandelt, wäre der Rechtsstreit vermieden worden** (If the parties had negotiated earlier, the lawsuit would have been avoided)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Structure of the main clause that follows",
     "texto": [
      "The main clause that follows the inverted condition must begin with the conjugated verb or with the correlative pronoun **so** followed immediately by the conjugated verb: **Wäre der Vertrag unterschrieben worden, (so) bestünde nun Rechtssicherheit**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "With wenn",
